{"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "inverse_mod", "ucas": "inverse 3 mod 256", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "inverse", "method": "extended Euclid: 171*3 - 2*256 = 1", "lhs": "3^-1", "modulus": "256", "value": "171", "value_int": 171, "headline": "3^-1 = 171 mod 256"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "3 * 171 = 513 = 2*256 + 1"}], "files": [], "text": "3^-1 = 171 mod 256\n  how: extended Euclid: 171*3 - 2*256 = 1\n  check: 3 * 171 = 513 = 2*256 + 1\n"}
{"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "inverse_mod", "ucas": "inverse 0x53 in GF(2^8, aes)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "inverse", "value": "0xca", "polynomial": "0xca = x^7 + x^6 + x^3 + x", "in": "GF(2^8, aes)", "method": "a^(q-2) (a^(q-1) = 1 for every nonzero a)", "headline": "0x53^-1 = 0xca = x^7 + x^6 + x^3 + x in GF(2^8, aes)"}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "integers are elements in integer notation (the coefficients as base-2 digits): 0x53 = x^6 + x^4 + x + 1"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "0x53 * 0xca = 0x01 (shift-and-add multiplication)"}], "files": [], "text": "  note: integers are elements in integer notation (the coefficients as base-2 digits): 0x53 = x^6 + x^4 + x + 1\n0x53^-1 = 0xca = x^7 + x^6 + x^3 + x in GF(2^8, aes)\n  how: a^(q-2) (a^(q-1) = 1 for every nonzero a)\n  check: 0x53 * 0xca = 0x01 (shift-and-add multiplication)\n"}
{"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring GF(2^8, aes) 0x57 * 0x83", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "method": "carry-less product 0x2b79, reduced mod (x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1), the AES (Rijndael) polynomial 0x11b", "headline": "0x57 * 0x83 = 0xc1 = x^7 + x^6 + 1 in GF(2^8, aes)"}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "integers are elements in integer notation (the coefficients as base-2 digits): 0x57 = x^6 + x^4 + x^2 + x + 1"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the same with a second multiplication algorithm (shift-and-add, xtime)"}], "files": [], "text": "  note: integers are elements in integer notation (the coefficients as base-2 digits): 0x57 = x^6 + x^4 + x^2 + x + 1\n0x57 * 0x83 = 0xc1 = x^7 + x^6 + 1 in GF(2^8, aes)\n  how: carry-less product 0x2b79, reduced mod (x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1), the AES (Rijndael) polynomial 0x11b\n  check: the same with a second multiplication algorithm (shift-and-add, xtime)\n"}
{"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring Z/12", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "a_field": "no; an integral domain: no (12 is not prime: 2 * 6 = 0 with both nonzero)", "crt": "Z/12 = Z/4 x Z/3 (a -> (a mod 4, a mod 3))", "units": "phi(12) = 4: 1, 5, 7, 11", "unit_group": "C2 x C2 (order 4, exponent lambda(12) = 2); not cyclic, so there is no primitive root", "zero_divisors": "7 nonzero (every nonzero non-unit of a finite ring): 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10", "nilpotents": "the multiples of rad(12) = 6, 2 of them: 0, 6", "idempotents": "2^2 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0, 1, 4, 9", "ideals": "(d) for each d | 12 (6 of them; Z/12 is a principal ideal ring): (1) (2) (3) (4) (6) (0)", "quotients": "Z/12 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)", "maximal": "prime ideals: (2), (3) (quotients Z/p, fields)", "lhs": "Z/12: the integers mod 12", "value": "2^2 * 3", "headline": "Z/12: the integers mod 12 = 2^2 * 3", "details": ["12 elements, characteristic 12"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "by brute force over the 12 elements: 4 units, 7 zero divisors, 2 nilpotents, 4 idempotents"}], "files": [], "text": "Z/12: the integers mod 12 = 2^2 * 3\n  12 elements, characteristic 12\n  a field: no; an integral domain: no (12 is not prime: 2 * 6 = 0 with both nonzero)\n  CRT: Z/12 = Z/4 x Z/3 (a -> (a mod 4, a mod 3))\n  units: phi(12) = 4: 1, 5, 7, 11\n  unit group: C2 x C2 (order 4, exponent lambda(12) = 2); not cyclic, so there is no primitive root\n  zero divisors: 7 nonzero (every nonzero non-unit of a finite ring): 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10\n  nilpotents: the multiples of rad(12) = 6, 2 of them: 0, 6\n  idempotents: 2^2 (e = 0 or 1 mod each prime power): 0, 1, 4, 9\n  ideals: (d) for each d | 12 (6 of them; Z/12 is a principal ideal ring): (1) (2) (3) (4) (6) (0)\n  quotients: Z/12 / (d) = Z/d (a -> a mod d)\n  maximal = prime ideals: (2), (3) (quotients Z/p, fields)\n  check: by brute force over the 12 elements: 4 units, 7 zero divisors, 2 nilpotents, 4 idempotents\n"}
{"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "crt", "ucas": "crt x = 2 mod 3, x = 3 mod 5", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "crt", "solutions": ["8"], "modulus": "15", "x": ["2 mod 3: x = 2", "2 (mod 3)", "3 mod 5: x = 3", "3 (mod 5)"], "method": "the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)", "headline": "the system", "more": ["x = 8 (mod 15)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution"}], "files": [], "text": "the system\n  x = 2 mod 3: x = 2\n    x = 2 (mod 3)\n  x = 3 mod 5: x = 3\n    x = 3 (mod 5)\nx = 8 (mod 15)\n  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)\n  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution\n"}
{"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 7 u32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^35 / 7) = 4908534053 (0x124924925, 33 bits), shift s = 3", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^35)", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*7 = 2^35 + e with e = 3 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer", "m_has_33_bits_one_more_than_u32": "the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x24924925 and an add that cannot overflow:", "c": "   t = mulhi(x, 0x24924925); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 2;", "in_ucas": "(u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 2", "headline": "x / 7 for unsigned x: u32"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 7 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)"}], "files": [], "text": "x / 7 for unsigned x: u32\n  m = ceil(2^35 / 7) = 4908534053 (0x124924925, 33 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^35)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*7 = 2^35 + e with e = 3 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer\n  m has 33 bits, one more than u32: the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x24924925 and an add that cannot overflow:\n    C:    t = mulhi(x, 0x24924925); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 2;\n    in ucas: (u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 2\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 7 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}
{"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring_factor", "ucas": "factor x^4 + 1 over GF(2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factor", "method": "square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)", "roots_in_gf_2": "1 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (1)", "lhs": "x^4 + 1", "over": "GF(2)", "value": "(x + 1)^4", "headline": "x^4 + 1 = (x + 1)^4 over GF(2)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin)"}], "files": [], "text": "x^4 + 1 = (x + 1)^4 over GF(2)\n  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)\n  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin)\n  roots in GF(2): 1 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (1)\n"}
{"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring_factor", "ucas": "factor 5 + 10i in Z[i]", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factor", "method": "the norm 125 = 5^3; 2 = -i (1 + i)^2 ramifies, p = 3 mod 4 stays prime, p = 1 mod 4 splits as gcd(p, t + i) with t^2 = -1 mod p and its conjugate", "lhs": "5 + 10i", "in": "Z[i]", "value": "(1 + 2i)^2 * (1 - 2i)", "headline": "5 + 10i = (1 + 2i)^2 * (1 - 2i) in Z[i]"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the product is the element; 1 is a unit (norm 1); each factor's norm is a prime or the square of a prime = 3 mod 4"}], "files": [], "text": "5 + 10i = (1 + 2i)^2 * (1 - 2i) in Z[i]\n  how: the norm 125 = 5^3; 2 = -i (1 + i)^2 ramifies, p = 3 mod 4 stays prime, p = 1 mod 4 splits as gcd(p, t + i) with t^2 = -1 mod p and its conjugate\n  check: the product is the element; 1 is a unit (norm 1); each factor's norm is a prime or the square of a prime = 3 mod 4\n"}
{"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "matrix", "ucas": "solve [[1, 2], [3, 4]] x = [1, 0] mod 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "solve", "method": "Gaussian elimination on [M | b]", "lhs": "x", "value": "(5, 5), the only solution", "headline": "x = (5, 5), the only solution"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "M x = b holds"}], "files": [], "text": "x = (5, 5), the only solution\n  how: Gaussian elimination on [M | b]\n  check: M x = b holds\n"}
