{"id": 23, "ok": true, "cmd": "irreducible", "ucas": "irreducible x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1 over GF(2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "irreducible", "method": "Rabin's test (degree 8: x^(q^8) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8; q = 2)", "headline": "x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 4: none divides"}], "files": [], "text": "x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 8: x^(q^8) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8; q = 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 4: none divides\n"}
{"id": 24, "ok": true, "cmd": "primitive", "ucas": "primitive x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1 over GF(2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "primitive", "method": ["Rabin's test (degree 8: x^(q^8) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8; q = 2)", "x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 3 * 5 * 17"], "headline": "x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)", "more": ["primitive: x has order 255 = q^8 - 1 = 255"], "details": ["so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 255 (maximal: every nonzero state)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 4: none divides"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 255"}], "files": [], "text": "x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)\n  how: Rabin's test (degree 8: x^(q^8) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8; q = 2)\n  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 4: none divides\nprimitive: x has order 255 = q^8 - 1 = 255\n  how: x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 3 * 5 * 17\n  so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 255 (maximal: every nonzero state)\n  check: stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 255\n"}
